# shellcheck shell=bash
# direnv sources this file with bash; the directive above says so to a
# linter run without `--shell=bash`, as `xnl lint` runs it (`scripts:B1`).
#
# direnv: enter the pinned toolchain automatically, so the tools you get are
# the tools CI gets. Entering also installs the git hooks (`scripts:C10`),
# which is why an ungated commit usually means a shell nobody entered.
#
# `use flake` and nothing else: any logic here would be shell living outside
# `scripts/` with no mirrored bats (`scripts:C13`), and the one file that
# bootstraps the gate is the worst place to keep an unchecked rule.
use flake
